From: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:06:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: Describe how Kairos task classes steer memory

The kairos controller's section says what CONFIG_KAIROS_MEMORY does with
a cgroup's class (reclaim, the allocator's reserves, the OOM killer) and
that memory is charged to the cgroup that first uses it;
kernel-parameters.txt lists kairos.nomemclass, which turns it off.

Signed-off-by: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst         | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
index 09a9b116d4dce6a3f35c959ae7ddbc88cada570b..6dc9896c2f76f0912b5c18fef8de2a9457d63223 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
@@ -2987,6 +2987,22 @@ The root cgroup is always "lc".
 	below it which inherits, down to the first one with a class of
 	its own.
 
+With the CONFIG_KAIROS_MEMORY config option the class also steers
+memory, unless "kairos.nomemclass" is on the kernel command line:
+
+- Reclaim passes over a latency-critical cgroup as if it were below its
+  "memory.low", against reclaim for the whole system or for a batch
+  cgroup above it.  A breach counts as a "low" event in its
+  "memory.events".
+- A latency-critical task may dip into the page allocator's reserves as
+  far as a realtime task, rather than stop to reclaim.
+- The OOM killer takes a batch task before any latency-critical one, as
+  if the batch task's "oom_score_adj" were 1000.
+
+Memory is charged to the cgroup of the task that first uses it, so a
+page which batch work brought into memory isn't protected when a
+latency-critical task uses it later.
+
 
 Non-normative information
 -------------------------
diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
index 9c163139a158fdb5274b164aa6bfa053d8d85d43..8f6b801d65bc27979d6993da40f27f4b8c969359 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
@@ -2900,6 +2900,12 @@ Kernel parameters
 	js=		[HW,JOY] Analog joystick
 			See Documentation/input/joydev/joystick.rst.
 
+	kairos.nomemclass
+			[KNL] Don't let Kairos task classes steer memory
+			(CONFIG_KAIROS_MEMORY): reclaim, the page allocator's
+			reserves and the OOM killer treat latency-critical
+			and batch tasks alike.
+
 	kairos.noscheduler
 			[KNL] Don't attach Kairos Scheduler before init
 			(CONFIG_KAIROS_BOOT_SCHEDULER). Kairos's init reads
